    <details class="mt-2" id="eos-materia-edit" @(Model.MateriaErrorMessage is not null ? "open" : "")>
        <summary class="small"><i class="fas fa-circle"></i> Add 5★ materia to a NeverCrisis account</summary>
        <div class="card card-body mt-2" style="max-width: 860px;">
            <p class="small mb-2">
                Build a list of 5★ materia with the sub stats you want, then download the updated <code>data\account.json</code>.
                <strong>Add maxed</strong> gives the top level with every stat at its best crafted roll and all level-up boosts (each at its highest) on the first stat.
                Refined materia have four fixed stats and stay at level 1.
            </p>
            <p class="small text-muted mb-2">
                Each stat works like crafting then leveling: the <em>crafted roll</em> is the stat when the materia is made, each level-up <em>boost</em> adds the amount per boost,
                and the result after "=" is the value you'll see in game.
                Which stats a recipe can roll comes from real accounts; recipes marked "estimated" copy a close recipe and may be off.
                Stop the server and back up <code>account.json</code> before replacing it. The file is read in memory and never saved.
            </p>
            <form method="post" enctype="multipart/form-data" asp-page-handler="SetMateria" id="eos-mat-form">
                <div class="mb-2">
                    <label class="form-label small mb-1" for="MateriaAccountFile">Server's account.json</label>
                    <input type="file" id="MateriaAccountFile" name="MateriaAccountFile" accept=".json,application/json" class="form-control form-control-sm" style="max-width: 420px;" required />
                    <div class="small mt-1" id="eos-mat-status"></div>
                </div>
                <div class="d-flex flex-wrap align-items-center gap-2 mb-2">
